# What docker is allowed to see when it builds the agent's box.
#
# The box gets its content by cloning from git remotes, never from this
# machine (ADR-0041 D1). So the build context is deny-by-default: the only
# file the image copies in is the check script, and everything else stays
# out. The rule that matters most is `projects/` — it holds the client
# repositories, and baking client source into an image layer is the exact
# opposite of what this image is for.
*
!docker/image-check.mjs

# Belt and braces. The list above already excludes these, but a later
# `!something` line could quietly let one back in, and .dockerignore is
# last-match-wins. These stay out whatever is added above them.
projects/
node_modules/
dist/
.timone/
.git/
daemon.log
*.png
.playwright-mcp/
